# Consumer hardware design package — verbatim vendor artifacts, verified
# byte-for-byte against omi/hardware/consumer/checksums.sha256. Any EOL
# normalization silently rewrites their bytes and breaks that check: it already
# corrupted omi-bom.csv, case-b.step and omi-device-charger-assembly.step on the
# original import (CRLF stripped, ~262 KB gone from the assembly STEP alone).
# Mark them binary so no checkout or commit can touch them again.
omi/hardware/consumer/**/*.step -text
omi/hardware/consumer/**/*.csv  -text
omi/hardware/consumer/**/*.zip  -text
omi/hardware/consumer/**/*.pdf  -text
omi/hardware/consumer/**/*.xlsx -text
